L72: Ratings of Perceived Exertion (RPE)
L73: Table  3  presents RPE data following each set of resistance exercise. No treatment effects were observed over all 6 sets and no significant treatments effects were observed for the mean session RPE [ P  = 0.18]. RPE obtained during each set was significantly [ P  < 0.001] negatively correlated with repetitions completed ( r  = −0.48 to −0.67). A significant time effect was observed between the 1st and 6th set of resistance exercise [ P  < 0.0001] where RPE values increased with each successive set. Table 3 Ratings of perceived exertion CT P S SCF Set 1 5.36 ± 1.5 5.18 ± 1.60 5.14 ± 1.27 5.41 ± 1.46 Set 2 6.55 ± 1.6 a 
